 - Updated the PostFX regression contract to verify the simplified Pencil controls and the new Float-Z sky mask.
 - The uploaded CI log came from commit `3ff4f01` and failed on the stale `camera movement removed` text assertion; that assertion is already absent in the current baseline (the follow-up `8f1740f` fix is included here).
+
+## Export naming cleanup + inline PostFX install instructions
+
+- Export defaults no longer leak technical preview/capture names such as `floatz_capture`, `bo3_depth_*_capture`, TOOLSGFX/runtime suffixes, or old APE hash suffixes into every generated asset name.
+- When a capture/debug filename is being used with generated Beginner HLSL, Shader Studio takes the first authored effect name as the friendly export base; Pencil Sketch therefore defaults to `pencil_sketch`.
+- Generic untouched Beginner names such as `New Screen Effect` also collapse to the first authored effect when possible. Explicit Base names typed by the user are still respected.
+- PostFX TOOLSGFX cache-busting files now use the cleaner `<base>_ape_<hash>.hlsl` form instead of `<prefix>_<base>_ape_<hash>.hlsl`. Direct Install cleans both old and new naming patterns so stale APE copies do not accumulate.
+- Shareable package ZIPs now default to `<base>_bo3.zip` instead of repeating the asset prefix in the archive name.
+- Derived image/sky asset names now use one de-duplicated prefix/base stem consistently.
+- `00_README_FIRST.txt` and direct-install `*_INSTALL_README.txt` now contain the full PostFX zone + client CSC activation steps and the exact generated copy/merge-ready CSC code. The separate `*_POSTFX_INTEGRATION.txt` remains only as a backup.
+- Generated install docs now explicitly describe the persistent slot-6 path and `filters::enable_filter_persistent()`.
